| explorer | hit | HEAD `4cafeea`: task selection by comma list at `benchmark/run.py:979-983,1040` and repo filter at `run.py:1095-1100`; `--modes` and `--experiment` already form a mutually exclusive group at `run.py:984-993`; `TASKS` lookups inside cells at `run.py:479,518`; per-row metadata merge at `run.py:1193-1202,1232`; local repo setup at `run.py:1113-1137`; registry at `benchmark/tasks/__init__.py:80-147`; repo languages at `benchmark/config.py:101,110-140`; manifest-validation pattern at `benchmark/variants.py:45-113`; results JSONL are gitignored (`.gitignore:37`), so the lock reads the c1 store, not result files |

## Approach

1. **Fixtures first.** Commit fixture panels under `benchmark/tests/fixtures/panels/`: one complete panel with three FeatureBench ids and the two SWE-bench Multilingual primaries, one complete panel using both fallbacks, and the malformed variants the tests parametrize. External ids resolve through stubbed c2 loaders and a stubbed `admit` in tests (F-1).
2. **Loader.** A new `benchmark/panels.py` parses the file, checks schema and family rules, resolves local members from `TASKS`, computes `stratify` and `split_digest`, and returns `Panel(name, cheap, dev, test, split_digest, members)` (G-2, G-3).
3. **Completeness and admission.** `panels.require_complete(panel, admit)` refuses missing required members and calls `external.preflight.admit` for each external member, refusing any non-admitted verdict (G-1, G-3, F-1).
4. **Run wiring.** `run.py` gains `--panel` and `--panel-split`. Inside `main`, after argument checks and before the MCP preflight, it loads the panel, runs `require_complete`, registers external tasks from `external.featurebench.load` and `external.swebench_ml.load` into `TASKS`, runs the split-lock check against the c1 store, and sets `tasks_list` to the selected members. The cell loop stamps `panel_name`, `panel_split_digest`, and `panel_split` into every row. External members run through c2 hooks with no container (F-1).
5. **Split lock.** `panels.check_split_lock(panel, rows)` refuses when a completed stored row with the same `panel_name` carries a different digest. `run.py` feeds it the c1 store rows.
6. **Commit the panel.** Run c2 preflight on the cook host, list the admitted FeatureBench Lite Level 1 instances, fill fallbacks only for primaries whose preflight fails (recording the reason), write `benchmark/panels/gepa-v1.json` through `panels.stratify`, and commit it before any paid run (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1).

## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            benchmark (existing harness) + new benchmark/panels.py and benchmark/panels/
spine step:       workflow (run.py task selection and cell loop)
public interface: panels.load_panel(path) -> Panel(name, cheap, dev, test, split_digest, members)  (G-2, G-3, F-1)
public interface: panels.require_complete(panel, admit) -> None; raises PanelError naming each missing or unadmitted member  (G-1, G-3, F-1)
public interface: panels.stratify(members, split_seed) -> dict[id, dev or test]; panels.check_split_lock(panel, rows) -> None  (G-2, G-3)
public interface: run.py --panel PATH --panel-split {cheap,dev,test,all}  (F-1)
consumed:         external.preflight.admit(instance_id) -> PreflightVerdict; external.featurebench.load / external.swebench_ml.load -> ExternalTask  (c2, F-1)
consumed:         c1 result store rows (read only) and completed-row rule  (c1)
private:          panel JSON schema, fallback pair table, digest canonicalization, stamp merge
crust delta:      new row fields panel_name, panel_split_digest, panel_split (not run-key inputs); new run.py flags; new benchmark/panels.py; new benchmark/panels/gepa-v1.json
arrows:           run.py -> panels -> tasks, external (preflight, loaders); panels -> baselines (row read); no container runtime anywhere on the path  (F-1)
```

## Acceptance
- AC-1: WHEN `run.py --panel PATH` is given a panel holding every required member with every external member admitted THE SYSTEM SHALL load it into `Panel(cheap, dev, test)` with the three local hard tasks in `cheap` and the stratified assignment in `dev` and `test`, resolve local members from `TASKS` and FeatureBench and SWE-bench Multilingual members through `external.featurebench.load` and `external.swebench_ml.load`, invoke the runner once per selected member, model, mode, and repetition for the `--panel-split` selection, and start no `docker`, `podman`, or other container process.  (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1)
- AC-2: WHEN a `run.py --panel` invocation loads a panel that lacks any one required member (at least one FeatureBench Lite Level 1 task, `gin_edit_render_context`, `rg_search_dispatch`, `rg_trait_implementors`, `gin_servehttp_flow`, the Go SWE-bench Multilingual slot, or the Rust SWE-bench Multilingual slot), or WHEN `external.preflight.admit` returns a non-admitted verdict for any external member, THE SYSTEM SHALL exit nonzero before any runner call and name each missing or unadmitted member.  (G-1, G-2, G-3, F-1)
- AC-3: WHEN a SWE-bench Multilingual slot is filled by its fallback THE SYSTEM SHALL accept it only when it carries `fallback_for` naming that slot's primary and a non-empty `fallback_reason`, include the fallback id in the split digest, and refuse a slot holding both its primary and fallback, a fallback paired with the other slot's primary, or a fallback without `fallback_for` or `fallback_reason`.  (G-3, F-1)
- AC-4: WHEN a panel loads THE SYSTEM SHALL keep exactly `rg_search_dispatch`, `rg_trait_implementors`, and `gin_servehttp_flow` in the cheap tier and out of `dev` and `test`, assign the other members by family-stratified alternation over `(language, sha256("<split_seed>:<id>"))`, and refuse a file whose recorded split differs from that assignment or that marks any other member `cheap`.  (G-2, G-3)
- AC-5: WHEN a panel run writes a row THE SYSTEM SHALL stamp `panel_name`, `panel_split_digest`, and `panel_split` outside the run key; WHEN a `run.py --panel` invocation finds a completed stored row with the same `panel_name` and a different `panel_split_digest` THE SYSTEM SHALL exit nonzero before any runner call; WHEN every completed stored row for that panel name carries the current digest, or none exists, or only error, quota, or timeout rows carry a different digest, THE SYSTEM SHALL proceed.  (G-1, G-2, G-3)
- AC-6: WHEN a panel file has an unknown key, a duplicate id, an unknown local task, a member outside the required families and ids, a local member whose language differs from its repo language, or an external task name that collides with a `TASKS` entry, or WHEN `--panel` is combined with a non-default `--tasks` or `--repos`, THE SYSTEM SHALL exit nonzero before any runner call and name the fault.  (G-2, G-3, F-1)
- AC-7: WHEN the committed `benchmark/panels/gepa-v1.json` is loaded THE SYSTEM SHALL return a panel holding at least one FeatureBench Lite Level 1 member, `gin_edit_render_context`, the three local hard tasks in the cheap tier, one Go and one Rust SWE-bench Multilingual slot member, and a recorded split equal to `panels.stratify` for its seed.  (G-1, G-2, G-3)

